From 83fd879cc85c7f93de28a4ddbec2d5b0a4d8e970 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:06:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Refresh priv_wrapper.keyring from keyservers/WKD: same certificate(s),
with self-signatures our copy was missing.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.
priv_wrapper.keyring was in the lookaside cache, which a pull request
cannot update, so it moves into git (dropped from sources).

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 .gitignore           |   1 -
 priv_wrapper.keyring | Bin 0 -> 18452 bytes
 priv_wrapper.spec    |   4 ++++
 sources              |   1 -
 4 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 priv_wrapper.keyring

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 823942f..242fed7 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -1,4 +1,3 @@
 /priv_wrapper-1.0.0.tar.gz
-/priv_wrapper.keyring
 /priv_wrapper-1.0.1.tar.gz
 /priv_wrapper-1.0.1.tar.gz.asc
diff --git a/priv_wrapper.keyring b/priv_wrapper.keyring
new file mode 100644
